Additional notice

This software is published for security research and for rooting hardware you
own. CVE-2026-43499 was publicly disclosed by NebuSec on 2026-07-07 and is
fixed upstream; this repository does not disclose a new vulnerability.

Running this against a device you do not own may be unlawful. Rooting voids
warranties, can trip Knox, and may break banking or DRM applications. A kernel
panic and automatic reboot is an expected failure mode of the exploit.

The third-party applications bundled in the release archive (Neo Backup,
App Manager, Shizuku) are the property of their respective authors and are
distributed under their own licenses.
